{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1c58d2ba-06e0-46ba-9ffc-0d60755e3e25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a03abc506726a1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-cttaqd16/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format\n\n## Description\n\nDefines the tutorial packaging format — tutorial metadata, pinned image\nreferences, and a validation manifest — so that tutorials are versioned and\ntestable independently of Dashboard releases. This format is the shared\ncontract consumed both by the Dashboard's tutorial gallery (to render and\nlaunch tutorials) and by tutorial authors (to package and validate tutorial\ncontent).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Specify the tutorial metadata structure: identity, the core journey a\n  tutorial covers, and the resources it expects in a user's project.\n- Define how a tutorial pins the images it runs on, so a tutorial executes\n  against known image versions rather than whatever is current at launch\n  time.\n- Define the validation manifest structure used to test a packaged tutorial\n  automatically.\n- Define the versioning scheme for the format itself, decoupled from\n  Dashboard release versioning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The format specification documents the metadata structure, the pinned-image\n  reference mechanism, and the validation manifest structure.\n- A tutorial packaged per the format carries a format version that is\n  independent of the Dashboard release version.\n- A packaged tutorial can be checked against its validation manifest with a\n  pass/fail result produced automatically.\n- The format supports all six core journeys (first workbench, data prep,\n  first training run, first pipeline, first deployment, first RAG app),\n  including both notebook-based tutorials and pipeline-based tutorials.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): tutorial packaging format — metadata, pinned images,\n  validation manifest; versioned and testable independently of Dashboard\n  releases. (Primary coverage.)\n- Indirectly enables HLR-1 (P0) and HLR-2 (P0): the gallery launch mechanics\n  and the curated tutorials both build against this format, which is why this\n  epic inherits P0 priority.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37271,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4d770febd292af1","agent_id":"a815ab71ef3d0efaa","session_id":"a958864d-502f-4687-961c-c18572f3c4be","uuid":"bad59f47-77de-45cf-be20-6f7038c51cad","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:00:19.091Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
