d-image\n55\t  reference mechanism, and the validation manifest structure.\n56\t- A tutorial packaged per the format carries a format version that is\n57\t  independent of the Dashboard release version.\n58\t- A packaged tutorial can be checked against its validation manifest with a\n59\t  pass/fail result produced automatically.\n60\t- The format supports all six core journeys (first workbench, data prep,\n61\t  first training run, first pipeline, first deployment, first RAG app),\n62\t  including both notebook-based tutorials and pipeline-based tutorials.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1): tutorial packaging format — metadata, pinned images,\n67\t  validation manifest; versioned and testable independently of Dashboard\n68\t  releases. (Primary coverage.)\n69\t- Indirectly enables HLR-1 (P0) and HLR-2 (P0): the gallery launch mechanics\n70\t  and the curated tutorials both build against this format, which is why this\n71\t  epic inherits P0 priority.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aeb5ca76f1535ca","agent_id":"a09cf324956fb8d96","session_id":"a958864d-502f-4687-961c-c18572f3c4be","uuid":"bb285276-96cd-42e5-bcd7-3cb7ac1548d1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:02:55.746Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d21108c416b5616","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
