rated and maintained as the platform evolves (the\n56\t  validation manifest is the mechanism that makes re-testing repeatable).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Six tutorials exist, one for each enumerated core journey.\n61\t- Each tutorial is packaged per the tutorial packaging format with metadata,\n62\t  pinned images, and a validation manifest.\n63\t- Each tutorial's validation manifest passes when executed against the\n64\t  current release — every tutorial runs end-to-end successfully on the\n65\t  current release.\n66\t- Each tutorial is launchable into a fresh user project and completes its\n67\t  journey without manual fix-up steps.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0): six curated tutorials covering the core journeys (first\n72\t  workbench, data prep, first training run, first pipeline, first deployment,\n73\t  first RAG app), each tested against the current release.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aeb5ca76f1535ca","agent_id":"a09cf324956fb8d96","session_id":"a958864d-502f-4687-961c-c18572f3c4be","uuid":"4b895dbf-18ad-487d-ae5f-7c26c9c66b52","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:02:59.323Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-806af3e6a7f406e7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
