mat and validation-manifest\n70\tstructure; E003 instantiates it per tutorial (consumes, does not redefine); E004\n71\tdocuments it. Data Science Pipelines is treated as passive with validation as\n72\tACs on E002, justified by the strategy assigning no separate owner. E003's size\n73\t(six notebook/pipeline tutorials plus manifests) is at the upper edge but within\n74\ta single sprint of content work; splitting by journey would fragment one logical\n75\tdeliverable (HLR-2). Team inference from architecture context is flagged as a\n76\thealth warning in the summary rather than silently asserted.\n77\t\n78\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n79\tNo Investigation epics were created — justified: the strategy states \"Open\n80\tQuestions: None\" and contains no conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks\n81\trequiring resolution; the summary documents this scan. All three Implementation\n82\tepics produce concrete artifacts (format spec + automated validation, gallery\n83\tsurface + launch mechanics, six packaged tutorials). E004 correctly carries\n84\t`implementation_type: docs-authoring`. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact`\n85\tfields are set anywhere, consistent with no gates existing.\n86\t\n87\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n88\tAll four epics are Implementation type and all four carry `ai_signals` (the\n89\t9-signal rubric) with `investigation_signals: null` — type-appropriate. Rationale\n90\tfiles exist for all four epics and their values match the frontmatter. Spot\n91\tchecks hold up: E001 `existing_foundation: -1` (no existing tutorial packaging\n92\tmechanism — greenfield) vs E002 `existing_foundation: +1` (extends the existing\n93\tGA odh-dashboard and its workbench-creation/pipeline-import flows) is a\n94\tconsistent distinction, corroborated by the architecture context. E001\n95\t`open_questions: +1` is consistent with the strategy's \"Open Questions: None\" —\n96\tthe remaining schema decisions are implementation detail, not scope-changing\n97\tu