G dependency. |\n100\t| E001, E002, E003 → E004 | 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes what was built — gallery usage and the contribution process — so it is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n101\t| No onboarding edges | 5–10, 20 | All components exist in the platform and are Konflux onboarded per architecture context; nothing new is provisioned. |\n102\t| No investigation edges | 3 | Strategy states \"Open Questions: None\"; no conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks requiring resolution before build. |\n103\t\n104\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n105\t\n106\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (summary) | Epic(s) |\n107\t|-----|----------|----------------------|---------|\n108\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Tutorial gallery in Dashboard with one-click launch into the user's project | E002 |\n109\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering core journeys, tested against current release | E003 |\n110\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) | E001 |\n111\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation for gallery usage and tutorial contribution | E004 |\n112\t\n113\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. No redundant/overlapping\n114\tHLR pairs — each HLR describes a distinct surface (format spec, gallery code,\n115\ttutorial content, documentation).\n116\t\n117\t## Health Warnings\n118\t\n119\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy omits the\n120\t  Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance\n121\t  criteria, and NFRs. Epic ACs were derived from HLRs; teams were inferred\n122\t  from architecture-context owning teams. Verify team assignments with the\n123\t  strategy author before execution.\n124\t- **Priority promotion note**: HLR-3 is labeled P1 in the strategy but its\n125\t  epic (E001) is P0 by priority inheritance — it gates all P0 work (gallery\n126\t  and tutorials). If the intent was for the gallery to ship with an\n127\t  ad-hoc tutorial layout and adopt the format later, the strategy should say\n128\t  so; as written, the format is the contract both P0 epics build against.\n129\t- **Moving-target risk on HLR-2**: \"tested against the current release\"\n130\t  requires re-validation at each release cadence; the validation manifest\n131\t  (E001/E003) is the mechanism that keeps this repeatable, but ongoing\n132\t  maintenance of the six tutorials is beyond this decomposition's epics.\n133\t- **Scope trap checked**: out-of-scope items (no community contribution\n134\t  tooling, no localization) are respected — the contribution process is\n135\t  documented only (E004 scope), and no intake tooling or translation work\n136\t  appears in any epic.\n137\t\n138\t## Tiered Delivery\n139\t\n140\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n141\tintra-platform.\n142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f490fc3b6037154","agent_id":"a1d2a30638b66cec6","session_id":"a958864d-502f-4687-961c-c18572f3c4be","uuid":"85817c9d-df5b-4a9d-a369-5b6664fac7e0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:07:21.074Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b09b686daa50eadd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
