ject.\n50\t- Notebook tutorials launch by opening a workbench in the user's project with\n51\t  the tutorial notebook loaded, honoring the tutorial's pinned images.\n52\t- Pipeline tutorials launch by importing the pipeline into the user's\n53\t  project.\n54\t- No code changes to the workbench (Notebooks) or Data Science Pipelines\n55\t  components: launch uses their existing, GA lifecycle and import behavior.\n56\t  Correct interaction with both is validated as acceptance criteria below.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a user with a project and an available tutorial, when the user\n61\t  launches the tutorial from the gallery, then it opens in their project — a\n62\t  workbench with the notebook loaded for notebook tutorials, or the pipeline\n63\t  imported for pipeline tutorials.\n64\t- The gallery renders tutorials from the tutorial packaging format's\n65\t  metadata, and launches honor the pinned images each tutorial declares.\n66\t- Launching a notebook tutorial creates a workbench via the existing\n67\t  workbench lifecycle with the notebook available in it (validates the\n68\t  Notebooks component keeps working unchanged).\n69\t- Launching a pipeline tutorial results in the pipeline being available in\n70\t  the user's project via existing Data Science Pipelines behavior (validates\n71\t  the Data Science Pipelines component keeps working unchanged).\n72\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be launched end-to-end in a test\n73\t  project without manual configuration steps beyond authentication.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): the Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n78\t  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the\n79\t  notebook, or importing the pipeline).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f490fc3b6037154","agent_id":"a1d2a30638b66cec6","session_id":"a958864d-502f-4687-961c-c18572f3c4be","uuid":"234efadf-a190-4f84-b186-f66b4d96e758","timestamp":"2026-1